<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Rim-Elves genes swapped for the equivalents other mods ship, with each retired gene going on this mod's
		Cherry Picker list.
		  - Alpha Genes: the elf's chemical susceptibility loses its toxic resistance factor (and drops from 5 to 3
		    metabolism to match), and the elf gains Alpha Genes' toxic vulnerability gene for that part instead.
		  - Big and Small: the elf's gigantism becomes Big and Small's large frame.
		  - Det's Stoneborn + VRE Pigskin: the elf's slow development becomes Pigskin's slow aging plus Stoneborn's
		    long lifespan; both mods are needed, as in the original.
		This folder only loads when Rim-Elves is active (see loadFolders.xml); each swap sits in a subfolder gated on the mod that supplies the replacement.
		Operations that also need another mod sit in a subfolder gated on it in loadFolders.xml.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: RE_Elve lists Size_Gigantism and Age_SlowDevelopment, both genes
		are Rim-Elves' own, RE_ChemicalSusceptibility ships biostatMet 5 with a ToxicResistance factor, and
		AG_ToxResist_Vulnerability, BS_LargeFrame, VRE_SlowAging and DV_LifespanLong all exist. The astrogene
		Cherry Picker entries name defs built at runtime, not in any XML: both Alpha Genes and VRE Starjack generate
		_Astrogene copies of other mods' genes.
		Fix 2026-10-03: a retired gene is now swapped in every xenotype that carries it (not just this mod's), and only
		retired under the same mods as its replacement. Before, other mods' xenotypes sharing the gene (and this one, when
		the replacement mod was absent) lost it to Cherry Picker with nothing in its place.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RE_Elve"]/genes</xpath>
		<value>
			<li>AG_ToxResist_Vulnerability</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/GeneDef[defName="RE_ChemicalSusceptibility"]/biostatMet</xpath>
		<value>
			<biostatMet>3</biostatMet>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
		<xpath>Defs/GeneDef[defName="RE_ChemicalSusceptibility"]/statFactors/ToxicResistance</xpath>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
